    summary: "These terms describe the sample and the process rather than a separate set of controls.",
    steps: ["Reagent: a chemical ingredient. Product: material formed by a reaction. Units (u): the amount of material. Ratio: proportions that scale together.", "Purity: quality of one chemical. Contamination: other chemicals mixed in. Catalyst: required material that survives the reaction.", "Buffer: an adjustment to pH. Route: how a chemical enters a body. Dose: the amount administered. Yield: how much useful product is retained."],
